codex
The A5 slice is narrower than it first looked: the IR only records dangerous sinks in `PrliAuthenticatorController`, while the other `init` callbacks mostly register UI, route bookmarklets, or dispatch redirects. I’m checking the authorization primitive and the redirect helpers now, because exploitability turns on whether those guards really bind the `init` handlers to privileged users and whether any redirect target is still attacker-controlled after the guard.
